      "problem": "Which of the following residue classes modulo $7$ contain the integer $-2?$\n\nI. $[1]_{7}$\n\nII. $[5]_{7}$\n\nIII. $[-9]_{7}$",
      "worked_solution": "We have $-2\\in [a]_{7}$ if \n\n$$\n-2≡a\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $-2\\notin [1]_{7}$ because $-2≢1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $-2\\in [5]_{7}$ because $-2≡5\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ $\\,✓$\n\n- $-2\\in [-9]_{7}$ because $-2≡-9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
